& [Requirements]
  + [CPRB-001] bind generation to the canonical repository published codex/self-hosted-corpus HEAD exact Cargo.lock and windows-x86_64 target identity
  + [CPRB-002] build cantor cantor-corpus cantord and cantorctl release binaries with locked offline dependencies or verify exact prebuilt workspace binaries
  + [CPRB-003] admit exactly four distinct regular binary source identities with checked nonzero size SHA256 and a 16 MiB per-entry ceiling
  + [CPRB-004] generate one strict bundle-manifest JSON with closed fields profile source commit target Cargo.lock identity ordered entries and explicit capability denials
  + [CPRB-005] generate one bounded operator README that identifies the archive as a provider-free portable release-bundle candidate and points to checked repository runbooks
  + [CPRB-006] create exactly six archive entries under one closed allowlist using normalized slash paths ordinal order no compression and the fixed ZIP DOS timestamp fields 1980-01-01 00:00:00
  + [CPRB-007] require every entry path to be relative normalized traversal-free duplicate-free nonempty and no more than 128 characters
  + [CPRB-008] construct into one absent workflow-owned staging directory under a physical output parent then atomically publish distinct ZIP and evidence JSON files
  + [CPRB-009] refuse existing outputs unless explicit replacement is selected and never delete or overwrite an output directory reparse target or aliased ZIP/report path
  + [CPRB-010] cap the complete archive at 16 MiB and publish exact archive manifest and entry byte and SHA256 identities without retaining executable content in JSON
  + [CPRB-011] independently verify the evidence JSON closed shape archive hash ZIP metadata exact allowlist and every entry hash and byte count without extracting or executing the archive
  + [CPRB-012] compare archived binary bytes to the current exact workspace release binaries and bind the reported source commit as an ancestor of current HEAD
  + [CPRB-013] verify the embedded manifest and operator README bytes are exactly rederived from the report rather than trusted from the archive
  + [CPRB-014] prove two independent generations from the same inputs are byte-identical
  + [CPRB-015] adversarially refuse archive corruption report hash drift unknown and missing entries duplicate or traversal entries target drift capability escalation and current-binary drift
  + [CPRB-016] retain one checked ZIP and evidence report in the governed experiment artifact directory
  + [CPRB-017] document generation verification contents intended handoff and exact nonclaims
  + [CPRB-018] update product readiness as one portable-package-identity step while leaving supported distribution installer trust configuration migration upgrade support operator and production acceptance open
  + [CPRB-019] pass focused generator verifier determinism adversarial PowerShell parse format recursive evidence attribution commit push and post-push gates
  + [CPRB-020] never install extract execute start a service create or retain keys tokens configuration corpus state or logs download dependencies contact a provider use remote fallback persist effects use remote FPGA or enter Minecraft scope

